---Calculates a linearly interpolated value based on starting and final values and an interpolation factor.
---
---Warning: The interpolation factor used must be in a 0..1 range for this to yield a valid result.
---@param start number Starting value used in interpolation.
---@param final number Final value used in interpolation.
---@param t number Interpolation percentage between start and end values.
---@return number # Resulting value from interpolating between start and end.
---@overload fun(start: Vector2, final: Vector2, t: number): Vector2
---@overload fun(start: Vector3, final: Vector3, t: number): Vector3
---@overload fun(start: Vector4, final: Vector4, t: number): Vector4
---@overload fun(start: Matrix33, final: Matrix33, t: number): Matrix33
function lerp(start, final, t) end

---Calculates a spherically interpolated value based on starting and final values and an interpolation factor.
---
---Info: This is generally used for rotations, where just using linear interpolation instead would yield non-normalised
---results, resulting in an invalid rotation value.
---
---Warning: The interpolation factor used must be in a 0..1 range for this to yield a valid result.
---@param start Vector3 Starting value used in interpolation.
---@param final Vector3 Final value used in interpolation.
---@param t number Interpolation percentage between start and end values.
---@return Vector3 # Resulting value from interpolating between start and end.
---@overload fun(start: Quaternion, final: Quaternion, t: number): Quaternion
function slerp(start, final, t) end

---Limits a value to the provided range.
---@param value number Value to clamp.
---@param min number Minimum value that can be returned.
---@param max number Maximum value that can be returned.
---@return number # The resulting value clamped to the provided min and max range.
function clamp(value, min, max) end

---Calculates a random value in the specified range.
---@param min number Minimum value that can be returned.
---@param max number Maximum value that can be returned.
---@return number # The randomly calculated value within the specified range
function random(min, max) end
